:[{"text":"தாழ்","lemma":"tāḦ","gloss":"decline/delay"},{"text":"ஆது","lemma":"ātu","gloss":"without"}],"gloss":"without delaying"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"செறுத்த","parts":[{"text":"செறுத்த","lemma":"செறுத்த","gloss":"well-knit"}],"gloss":"well-knit","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"செய்யுள்","parts":[{"text":"செய்யுள்","lemma":"ceyyuḷ","gloss":"poetry"}],"gloss":"poetry"},{"surface":"செய்","parts":[{"text":"செய்","lemma":"cey","gloss":"make"}],"gloss":"composing"},{"surface":"செந்","parts":[{"text":"செந்","lemma":"செந்","gloss":"excellent"}],"gloss":"excellent","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நாவின்","parts":[{"text":"நா","lemma":"nā","gloss":"tongue"},{"text":"இன்","lemma":"iṉ","gloss":"of"}],"gloss":"of the tongue"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வெறுத்த","parts":[{"text":"வெறுத்த","lemma":"வெறுத்த","gloss":"abundant"}],"gloss":"abundant","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கேள்வி","parts":[{"text":"கேள்வி","lemma":"kēḷvi","gloss":"learning"}],"gloss":"learning"},{"surface":"விளங்கு","parts":[{"text":"விளங்கு","lemma":"viḷaṅku","gloss":"shine"}],"gloss":"shining"},{"surface":"புகழ்க்","parts":[{"text":"புகழ்க்","lemma":"புகழ்க்","gloss":"fame"}],"gloss":"fame","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கபிலன்","parts":[{"text":"கபிலன்","lemma":"kapilaṉ","gloss":"Kapilaṉ"}],"gloss":"Kapilaṉ"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"இன்று","parts":[{"text":"இன்று","lemma":"iṉṟu","gloss":"today"}],"gloss":"today"},{"surface":"உளன்","parts":[{"text":"உள்","lemma":"uḷ","gloss":"exist"},{"text":"அன்","lemma":"aṉ","gloss":"he"}],"gloss":"he is present"},{"surface":"ஆயின்","parts":[{"text":"ஆயின்","lemma":"āyiṉ","gloss":"if"}],"gloss":"if"},{"surface":"நன்று","parts":[{"text":"நன்று","lemma":"naṉṟu","gloss":"good"}],"gloss":"good"},{"surface":"மன்","parts":[{"text":"மன்","lemma":"maṉ","gloss":"particle of regret"}],"gloss":"indeed (regret)"},{"surface":"என்ற","parts":[{"text":"என்ற","lemma":"என்ற","gloss":"who said"}],"gloss":"who said","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"நின்","parts":[{"text":"நின்","lemma":"niṉ","gloss":"your"}],"gloss":"your"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"ஆடு","parts":[{"text":"ஆடு","lemma":"āṭu","gloss":"victory"}],"gloss":"victory"},{"surface":"கொள்","parts":[{"text":"கொள்","lemma":"koḷ","gloss":"receive"}],"gloss":"receiving"},{"surface":"வரிசைக்கு","parts":[{"text":"வரிசை","lemma":"varicai","gloss":"honor"},{"text":"க்கு","lemma":"kku","gloss":"to"}],"gloss":"to the honor"},{"surface":"ஒப்ப","parts":[{"text":"ஒப்ப","lemma":"oppa","gloss":"to match"}],"gloss":"to match"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பாடுவன்","parts":[{"text":"பாடு","lemma":"pāṭu","gloss":"sing"},{"text":"அன்","lemma":"aṉ","gloss":"I"}],"gloss":"I will sing"},{"surface":"மன்னால்","parts":[{"text":"மன்","lemma":"maṉ","gloss":"indeed"},{"text":"ஆல்","lemma":"āl","gloss":"particle"}],"gloss":"indeed"},{"surface":"பகைவரை","parts":[{"text":"பகைவர்","lemma":"pakaivar","gloss":"enemies"},{"text":"ஐ","lemma":"ai","gloss":"accusative case marker"}],"gloss":"enemies"},{"surface":"கடப்பே","parts":[{"text":"கடப்பு","lemma":"kaṭappu","gloss":"conquering"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"conquering"}]}],"literal":"Mature long pearl oysters on the wide sand / ray-emitting gems of eye-dazzling mansions / shining bangled women on the terrace play / illustrious excellence of Viḷaṅkil distress destroyed / battlefield-taking elephants and swift horses O Poṟaiya / if expanded it widens, if condensed it falls short / bewildered heart of people like us certainly / is not fully graspable your fame indeed always / illustrious people born in this wide world / we will not live saying so is difficult indeed without delaying / well-knit poetry making excellent tongue / abundant learning shining fame Kapilaṉ / today if he were present it would be good indeed, who said, your / victory-receiving honor to match / I will sing indeed, enemies conquering.","translation":"O Poṟaiya, lord of battle-ready elephants and swift horses, who destroyed the distress of the illustrious and prosperous town of Viḷaṅkil—where women wearing shining bangles play on the terraces of mansions adorned with eye-dazzling, ray-emitting gems, near the wide sands rich with mature pearl oysters! If one tries to expand upon your fame, it grows endlessly; if one tries to condense it, it falls short. For those of us with bewildered hearts, your fame is always beyond full grasp. Yet, in this wide world where illustrious men are born, it is hard for us to say we cannot live. You once said, 'If Kapilaṉ—of the excellent tongue that composed well-knit poetry, of abundant learning and shining fame—were alive today, how good it would be!' To match that high standard of appreciation you showed, I shall sing of your victories over your enemies.","modern":"முதிர்ந்த சிப்பிகள் முத்துக்களைத் தரும் நீண்ட மணற்பரப்பையும், கதிர்களை வீசும் மணிகள் பதிக்கப்பட்ட மாடங்களையும் உடைய விளங்கு சீர் கொண்ட விளங்கில் என்னும் ஊரின் துன்பத்தைத் துடைத்த, போர்க்களத்தில் பகைவரைக் கொல்லும் யானைகளையும் வேகமான குதிரைகளையும் உடைய பொறையனே! உன்னுடைய புகழை விரித்துச் சொன்னால் அது பெருகிக்கொண்டே போகும்; சுருக்கிச் சொன்னால் அது முழுமையாகாது. இதனால் கலக்கமடைந்த நெஞ்சத்தை உடைய எங்களைப் போன்றவர்களுக்கு உனது புகழை முழுமையாகப் பாடி முடிப்பது இயலாத ஒன்று. அறிவுடைய சான்றோர்கள் பிறந்த இந்த அகன்ற உலகத்தில் நாம் வாழமாட்டோம் என்று சொல்வதும் அரிது. செப்பமான செய்யுள்களைச் செய்யும் செந்நாவையும், மிகுந்த கேள்வியறிவையும், விளங்கும் புகழையும் உடைய கபிலன் இன்று உயிரோடு இருந்திருந்தால் எவ்வளவு நன்றாக இருக்கும் என்று நீ கூறினாய். உன்னுடைய அந்த உயர்ந்த தகுதிக்கு ஏற்ப, உனது பகைவர்களை வெல்லும் வெற்றியை நான் பாடுவேன்.","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Vākai tiṇai (victory and praise) and the Arasavākai tuṟai, which celebrates the virtues and achievements of a king. The poet Poruntil Iḷaṅkīraṉār addresses the Chera king Māntarañcēral Irumpoṟai. The king had expressed a deep regret that the legendary poet Kapilaṉ was no longer alive to witness and sing of his greatness. The poet beautifully responds to this by stating that the king's fame is so vast that any attempt to describe it either becomes too long or falls short of its true scale. However, inspired by the king's high regard for Kapilaṉ, the poet promises to sing of the king's victories over his enemies in a manner worthy of that high standard. The opening lines describe the prosperous town of Viḷaṅkil, establishing the king's role as a protective and benevolent ruler.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.55],[0.55,0.87],[0.87,1.2],[1.2,1.5],[1.5,1.7],[1.7,2.48],[2.48,3.1],[3.1,3.81],[3.81,4.23],[4.3,5.1],[5.1,5.4],[5.4,5.6],[5.6,5.8],[5.8,6.2],[6.2,7.4],[7.4,7.7],[7.7,7.9],[7.9,8.3],[8.3,8.8],[8.8,9.93],[9.93,10.6],[10.6,10.9],[10.9,11.2],[11.2,11.92],[11.92,12.5],[12.5,13.0],[13.0,13.5],[13.5,14.12],[14.12,14.9],[14.9,15.4],[15.4,15.9],[15.9,16.54],[16.54,17.18],[17.18,17.66],[17.66,18.3],[19.4,19.83],[20.0,20.6],[20.6,21.0],[21.0,21.5],[21.5,22.3],[22.3,22.8],[22.8,23.0],[23.0,23.3],[23.3,24.7],[24.7,25.1],[25.1,25.48],[25.62,26.0],[26.0,26.9],[26.9,27.22],[27.22,28.08],[28.08,28.5],[28.5,29.5],[29.5,29.9],[29.9,30.3],[30.3,30.5],[30.5,30.9],[30.9,31.3],[31.3,31.58],[31.58,32.28],[32.28,32.69],[32.69,33.09],[33.09,33.5],[33.5,33.9],[34.0,34.6]],"female":[[0.0,0.8],[0.8,1.06],[1.06,1.32],[1.32,1.5],[1.5,1.7],[1.7,2.42],[2.42,3.0],[3.0,3.6],[3.6,4.2],[4.2,4.8],[4.8,5.2],[5.2,5.4],[5.4,5.6],[5.6,6.0],[6.0,7.3],[7.3,7.5],[7.5,7.96],[7.96,8.32],[8.32,8.6],[8.6,9.66],[9.66,10.3],[10.3,10.6],[10.6,10.9],[10.9,11.73],[11.73,12.4],[12.4,12.9],[12.9,13.4],[13.4,14.02],[14.02,14.8],[14.8,15.3],[15.3,15.8],[15.8,17.22],[17.5,17.9],[17.9,18.2],[18.2,18.4],[19.56,19.99],[20.16,20.76],[20.76,21.16],[21.16,21.66],[21.66,22.46],[22.46,22.96],[22.96,23.16],[23.16,23.46],[23.46,24.18],[24.43,24.67],[24.67,25.15],[25.15,26.36],[26.36,27.56],[27.56,27.96],[27.96,29.03],[29.03,29.36],[29.36,29.56],[29.56,30.0],[30.0,30.74],[30.74,31.86],[31.86,32.36],[32.36,32.76],[32.76,32.96],[32.96,33.73],[33.73,34.34],[34.34,34.7],[34.7,35.06],[35.06,35.